{
 "_doc": "Wilderness set piece, round 5, tier 2, wilderness pool (site forest): a family's treehouses in three big firs. Plank huts on decks at 3.15 m (the kitchen hut, the bunk hut) and 6.15 m (the nest) round the trunks, joined by rope bridges, stood on peeled stilts; reached only by real ladders through deck trapdoors. Route: the deer-fenced garden and the kitchen tree's pulled-up front ladder -> the burned cabin (a chime on the door; the ones the fire didn't finish: ambush on entering) -> out its burned-out back wall -> round the back of the big fir (jaws in the needles) -> up the back ladder to the main deck -> the east bridge to the bunk hut, shut on them from the bridge side (Hal and Curtis: ambush on the door) -> back over the main deck and the west bridge's loose boards (they wake the kitchen) -> the kitchen hut (Marnie, the tree rules, the nest key) -> up the nest ladder to the padlocked nest (a shotgun on its wire inside) -> Dale (guardian) and the stores chest (loot) -> down to the main deck and through the shed's trapdoor -> the shed door bolted from inside, out. Hollowed can't climb: the decks were safe until hunger brought the family down. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
